{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2530,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Astrobiologist Michael Russell once said that\n“the purpose of life is to hydrogenate carbon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7690,
    "dDurationMs": 1119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dioxide.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8809,
    "dDurationMs": 4221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or as Nobel prize-winning physiologist Albert\nSzent-Györgyi put it, “life is nothing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13030,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but an electron looking for a place to rest.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15570,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While these aphorisms might not capture the\n“meaning of life” that most of us look"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19130,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for, their point is that living organisms\nultimately depend on and facilitate the universe’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24810,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tendency to increase entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26770,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That may seem counter-intuitive, since living\nbeings are themselves highly organized, while"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31310,
    "dDurationMs": 1870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entropy is a measure of disorder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33180,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as we know, complexity is not the same\nthing as order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36730,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every organism, just by living and breathing,\nacts to increase the entropy of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42030,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think of a photon arriving from the Sun, packed\nwith useful energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45030,
    "dDurationMs": 5189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It can be captured by a plant or microorganism\nthat uses photosynthesis to store that energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50219,
    "dDurationMs": 1401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the form of sugar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51620,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the sugar doesn’t contain quite as much\nuseful energy as the original photon – some"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55730,
    "dDurationMs": 3129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the energy ends up heating the plant and\nits environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58859,
    "dDurationMs": 6431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An animal like us eats the sugar, and uses\nits energy to create molecules of ATP, adenosine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65290,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "triphosphate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66290,
    "dDurationMs": 4649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ATP is like a little power-pack of energy\nthat can be sent to a part of the body where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70939,
    "dDurationMs": 4591,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it might be helpful, but ATP doesn’t have\nquite as much useful energy as the sugar that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75530,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "went into making it – some of that useful\nenergy got lost pushing around all the cell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79740,
    "dDurationMs": 1870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "machinery that makes the ATP."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81610,
    "dDurationMs": 5350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The proteins in your muscles utilize the energy\nin ATP to contract, so that you can lift a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86960,
    "dDurationMs": 2019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "barbell or a slice of pizza."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88979,
    "dDurationMs": 4871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But not all of the useful energy of the ATP\ngoes into lifting the pizza – as before,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93850,
    "dDurationMs": 2809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some of it is degraded into noise and heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96659,
    "dDurationMs": 5771,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only that, ATP’s useful energy can also\nbe used to repair broken-down cells or organs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102430,
    "dDurationMs": 2210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "again becoming less useful in the process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104640,
    "dDurationMs": 5269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The pattern here is obvious: every step along\nthe way, the energy in that original photon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109909,
    "dDurationMs": 5541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is gradually degraded, entropy increases,\nand at the end all that’s left is an organized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115450,
    "dDurationMs": 5019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but slightly warmer plant and cell and muscle,\nplus some high-entropy infrared light that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120469,
    "dDurationMs": 2541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gets radiated out into the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123010,
    "dDurationMs": 5650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Energy transforms from useful to useless in\nthe cause of keeping organisms like us alive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128660,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, life itself might have arisen because\nof entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132340,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The early Earth had pockets of low-entropy\nconditions full of useful energy, like warm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136980,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alkaline vents on the ocean floor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139040,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there may have been no simple chemical\nreaction that could take advantage of that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142810,
    "dDurationMs": 3149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy, use up its usefulness, and allow the\nentropy to increase."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145959,
    "dDurationMs": 4221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There were, however, more complicated chains\nof reactions that could do the job."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150180,
    "dDurationMs": 4699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In just the right circumstances, an appropriate\nnetwork of chemical reactions might find a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154879,
    "dDurationMs": 4351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way to sustain itself by tapping into the\nuseful energy in its environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159230,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some networks might have become embedded in\nmolecular membranes, the precursors of cell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163810,
    "dDurationMs": 5069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "walls, and broken away from their point of\norigin, becoming the first “living” organisms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168879,
    "dDurationMs": 5521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe that's how life began: a complex combination\nof chemical reactions that figured out how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174400,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to tap into otherwise unavailable useful energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178030,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can tell a similar story about why stars\nshine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181380,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hydrogen nuclei have a ton of useful, low-entropy\nnuclear energy to release -- if you can get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185980,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them to fuse together into helium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187900,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there’s a big barrier to getting that\nto happen – fusion is hard!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191580,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, the cores of stars do the job marvelously,\nso stars, like life, also survive because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198060,
    "dDurationMs": 2899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the increase of entropy throughout the\nuniverse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200959,
    "dDurationMs": 8691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our sun takes a low-entropy fuel source and\nconverts it into higher entropy energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209650,
    "dDurationMs": 5610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Life takes that higher-entropy energy as a\nfuel source and converts it into even higher-entropy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215260,
    "dDurationMs": 2839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218099,
    "dDurationMs": 6890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a very real sense, the purpose of life\nis to continue the mission of the stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224989,
    "dDurationMs": 3441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, Henry here, thanks for watching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228430,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the fifth video in a series about\ntime and entropy made in collaboration with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232020,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physicist Sean Carroll."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233530,
    "dDurationMs": 4319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This final video is supported by Audible.com,\na leading provider of audiobooks including"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237849,
    "dDurationMs": 1921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fiction, non-fiction and periodicals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239770,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The videos in this series are based off of\nSean’s book “The Big Picture: On the Origins"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243530,
    "dDurationMs": 4629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Life, Meaning, and the Universe Itself,”\nwhich is available, read by him, on Audible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248159,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can listen to “The Big Picture” or\nanother book of your choice – but really,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251319,
    "dDurationMs": 4271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "check out “The Big Picture” – for free,\nwith a free 30-day trial at Audible.com/minutephysics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255590,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, that’s audible.com/minutephysics."
    } ]
  } ]
}
